# Website Package Dependency

Doc site (`evergreen-design-system-doc`) **only** imports from three published packages in sibling repo `evergreen-design-system-website`:

| Package | Path | What to import |
|---------|------|----------------|
| `@evergreen/tokens` | `packages/tokens` | CSS variables (`@import '@evergreen/tokens'`), `liquid-glass`, `corner-smoothing` |
| `@evergreen/components` | `packages/components` | Vue UI primitives (Button, Input, NavBar, …) when doc needs live previews |
| `@evergreen/scenes` | `packages/scenes` | Composed marketing/business blocks when doc needs scene demos |

Link in `package.json` (add components/scenes when needed):

```json
"@evergreen/tokens": "link:../evergreen-design-system-website/packages/tokens"
```

Dev rebuild: `plugins/evergreen-tokens-dev.ts` watches `packages/tokens/spec/`. `predev` / `prebuild` run `build:tokens` in website repo.

## Do NOT import from website

- Website repo has **no app layer** — only `packages/*`. Never deep-import website source paths.
- Do not point any `@evergreen/*` at `evergreen-design-system-desktop`.
- Do not copy token/component/scene **source** into doc — consume built packages.

## Doc-owned (stays in this repo)

Everything that is not the three packages above lives under `src/`:

| Concern | Location |
|---------|----------|
| App shell & doc chrome | `src/layouts/`, `src/components/AppRail`, `SectionNav`, `PageToc`, `BrandSwitcher`, `DocMetaPanel`, … |
| Markdown pipeline | `src/markdown/` |
| Motion | `src/motion/` |
| Theme | `src/composables/useTheme*.ts` |
| Person avatar | `src/personAvatar/` |
| Doc content | `src/content/docs/` |
| Router & nav config | `src/router/`, `src/config/` |
| Shell hardcoded colors | `src/styles/global.css` |
| Legacy token name aliases | `src/styles/token-aliases.css` |
| BlockSuite editor | `src/components/DocEditor/` |

When adding a feature, ask: **is it a reusable design-system primitive or scene?** → website package. **Is it doc-site-specific?** → this repo.
